# Release quality gates

Record release status in `.cursor/experience-memory/release-scorecard.md`. No category complete without evidence.

## Visual gate

- [ ] Approved art direction preserved (`approved-direction.md`)
- [ ] No generic template residue (`anti-ai-slop.mdc`)
- [ ] Strong typography (`typography-director`)
- [ ] Intentional responsive compositions (`responsive-art-director`)
- [ ] No obvious spacing defects (`pixel-perfect-quality.mdc`)
- [ ] Dark and light themes complete if both supported
- [ ] No broken images or icons
- [ ] No visible placeholder content (`content-realism-editor`)

## Functional gate

- [ ] Primary journeys work end to end (`critical-user-journeys.md`)
- [ ] Forms validate; errors preserve useful state
- [ ] Destructive actions protected
- [ ] Navigation has no dead ends
- [ ] Buttons and links perform stated action
- [ ] Auth transitions work (when implemented)
- [ ] Billing transitions work (when implemented)
- [ ] Permission boundaries work
- [ ] Upgrade paths work
- [ ] Email actions work (when implemented)

## State gate

Per `state-completeness.mdc`:

- [ ] Empty, loading, error, success states complete on critical surfaces
- [ ] Restricted/plan states complete where billing exists
- [ ] Mobile and reduced-motion variants tested

## Quality gate

- [ ] Type checking passes
- [ ] Linting passes
- [ ] Tests pass (where applicable)
- [ ] No known hydration errors
- [ ] No avoidable console errors
- [ ] No major accessibility failures
- [ ] No major performance regressions (`performance-budget.md`)
- [ ] No horizontal mobile overflow
- [ ] No major layout shift
- [ ] No secret or environment-variable exposure in client bundle

## Experience gate

- [ ] First-time user understands product within 10 seconds
- [ ] Primary value demonstrated quickly
- [ ] Onboarding has clear completion (`onboarding-activation-architect`)
- [ ] Users always know what happens next
- [ ] Critical workflows have useful feedback
- [ ] Cohesive across marketing, auth, onboarding, product, billing, support, email

## Production review skills

Before release, invoke in fresh context where possible:

- `cross-browser-qa-engineer`
- `maintainability-critic`
- `visual-qa-critic`
- `layout-perfection-critic`

Implementing agent alone does not approve release.

## Vertical slice gate

Do not scale across all routes until the **complete vertical slice** passes (see `DESIGN_WORKFLOW.md`). Slice must include marketing entry, CTA, signup/demo, onboarding step, core action, loading, success, error/recovery, upgrade/next path, mobile, analytics, a11y, screenshot review.

## Experience scoring

Score each critical journey 1–10 on: immediate comprehension, product-value communication, interaction clarity, feedback, state completeness, recovery, perceived speed, trust, accessibility, mobile quality, visual polish, content realism, conversion clarity, technical stability.

**Any critical category below 9 triggers another pass** unless documented external constraint in `release-scorecard.md`.

A beautiful page with incomplete functionality does not pass.
A functional workflow with confusing presentation does not pass.
A polished desktop with weak mobile does not pass.
